  "content": {
    "id": "p19-ex2e-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Convert these mixed numerals to decimals, then put them in increasing order.\n\n$4\\frac{3}{4},\\ 4\\frac{3}{5},\\ 4\\frac{31}{100},\\ 4\\frac{5}{8}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4.31<4.6<4.625<4.75$\n\nThus $4\\frac{31}{100}<4\\frac{3}{5}<4\\frac{5}{8}<4\\frac{3}{4}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4\\frac{3}{4}&=4\\frac{75}{100}=4.75\\\\4\\frac{3}{5}&=4\\frac{6}{10}=4.6\\\\4\\frac{31}{100}&=4.31\\\\4\\frac{5}{8}&=4\\frac{625}{1000}=4.625\\end{align*}$$\nCompare corresponding digits from left to right:\n$$4.31<4.6<4.625<4.75.$$\nTherefore,\n$$4\\frac{31}{100}<4\\frac{3}{5}<4\\frac{5}{8}<4\\frac{3}{4}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
